<title>USA: Valero, Coastal win DOE's Elk Hills natgas bid.</title>
<headline>Valero, Coastal win DOE's Elk Hills natgas bid.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Valero Energy and Coastal Gas Marketing were the low bidders for 90,300 million British thermal units per day (mmBtu) of natural gas from the U.S. Naval Petroleum Reserve at Elk Hills, Calif., the Department of Energy said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The auction was for gas delivered between January 1, 1997 and March 1.</p>
<p>Valero bid $0.0210 over the monthly reference price for 60,000 mmBtus, while Coastal's premium was $0.0138 for 30,300 mmBtus.</p>
<p>The monthly reference price for December was $3.65 per mmBtu.</p>
<p>Other bidders were Western Gas at $0.0120, Pan Energy at $0.0060. NGC and Ensource bid at discounts to the reference price.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
